---
import DocsLayout from "../_components/DocsLayout.bangala"
import CodeBlock from "../_components/CodeBlock.bangala"

const anatomy = [
  "---",
  'import Card from "../components/Card.bangala"',
  "const posts = await db.posts.recent()",
  "---",
  "<h1>{posts.length} posts</h1>",
  '<Card title="Latest">',
  "  <p>HTML first. JavaScript when you ask.</p>",
  "</Card>",
].join("\n");

const controlFlow = `{#if posts.length === 0}
  <p>No posts yet.</p>
{:else}
  <ul>
    {#each posts as post}
      <li>{post.title}</li>
    {/each}
  </ul>
{/if}`;

const component = [
  "---",
  'import Card from "../components/Card.bangala"',
  "---",
  '<Card title="Hello" highlighted={true}>',
  "  <p>This goes into the default slot.</p>",
  "</Card>",
].join("\n");

const island = `<Counter start={10} client:load />
<Newsletter client:idle />
<Comments postId={post.id} client:visible />`;

const headings = [
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy" },
  { id: "frontmatter", label: "Frontmatter" },
  { id: "expressions", label: "Expressions" },
  { id: "control-flow", label: "Control flow" },
  { id: "components", label: "Components" },
  { id: "client-directives", label: "Client directives" },
];
---
<DocsLayout
  title=".bangala syntax | bangala.js"
  description="Reference de la syntaxe .bangala : frontmatter, expressions, control flow, composants, slots et client directives."
  path="/docs/syntax"
  section="Core Concepts"
  lead=".bangala is HTML with a small template layer. No JSX, no virtual DOM, no client runtime unless you mark an island."
  headings={headings}
  prev={{ href: "/docs/project-structure", label: "Project structure" }}
  next={{ href: "/docs/islands", label: "Islands Architecture" }}
>
  <h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>
  <p>A file has optional JavaScript frontmatter between <code>---</code> fences, followed by an HTML-first template body.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="pages/index.bangala" code={anatomy}/>

  <h2 id="frontmatter">Frontmatter</h2>
  <p>Frontmatter runs inside the generated async <code>render(props)</code> function. Use it for imports, local variables, <code>await</code>, and reading <code>props</code>. Exported declarations such as <code>getStaticPaths()</code> are hoisted to module scope.</p>

  <h2 id="expressions">Expressions</h2>
  <p><code>{`{expression}`}</code> inserts a JavaScript expression into HTML and escapes the result. This protects text and attribute values from markup injection by default.</p>
  <div class="docs-callout">
    <p>There is no raw HTML interpolation escape hatch in v1.0. If you need markup, write markup in the template rather than returning it from a string.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="control-flow">Control flow</h2>
  <p>Use <code>{`{#if}`}</code>, <code>{`{:else}`}</code>, and <code>{`{#each}`}</code> for server-side branching and loops.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="control-flow.bangala" code={controlFlow}/>

  <h2 id="components">Components</h2>
  <p>A capitalized tag maps to a default import. Static attributes become string props; bracketed attributes are JavaScript expressions. A component places children with <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="pages/index.bangala" code={component}/>

  <h2 id="client-directives">Client directives</h2>
  <p>Add a <code>client:*</code> directive to turn a server-rendered component into a browser island.</p>
  <CodeBlock filename="islands.bangala" code={island}/>
</DocsLayout>
